Answer FileProvider's APFS directory-statistics commands on HFS+ the way APFS answers for an item without them, so
new files in On My iPhone can be tracked (Safari downloads). With 1145 the lookup of Safari's .download placeholder
still failed with ENOTTY; 1146's tracer named it: LocalStorageFileProvider ffsctl cmd=0x80084a02 =
_IOW('J', 2, uint64_t), FileProvider's fpfs_pkg_enable_dirstat(). fpfs_track_document() (fchflags UF_TRACKED, then
this) fails on any error except EINVAL, APFS's answer for a file. FileProvider's package check (+0x17eb8) enables
them on a package directory (EINVAL fatal there, other errors skip the package handling), then fpfs_pkg_promote()
(xattr, Finder info) and fpfs_pkg_dirstat(); the document id lookup (+0xe7d5c) reads a directory's statistics with
ffsctl(_IOWR('J', 32, 40 bytes)) (0xc0284a20, fpfs_get_dirstat()) and accepts ENOTSUP. FileProviderDaemon's volume
code turns any error of either into a logged NSError, as with ENOTTY before. So: 'J' 2 is a no-op success on a
directory and EINVAL on anything else, 'J' 32 is ENOTSUP.

diff --git a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c b/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
--- a/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
+++ b/bsd/sweet_hfs/core/hfs_readwrite.c
@@ -3186,6 +3186,23 @@
 	case SWEET_APFSIOC_GET_PRISTINE_INFO:
 		bzero(ap->a_data, 2 * sizeof(uint64_t));
 		return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * Directory statistics. fpfs_track_document() (every item FileProvider tracks) first enables them,
+	 * ffsctl(_IOW('J', 2, uint64_t)) (fpfs_pkg_enable_dirstat()), and fails on any error but EINVAL, which is what
+	 * APFS answers for a file; FileProvider's package check (+0x17eb8) enables them on a package directory and then
+	 * promotes it. The document id lookup after it (+0xe7d5c) reads a directory's statistics, ffsctl(_IOWR('J', 32,
+	 * 40 bytes)) (dirstat), and accepts ENOTSUP. HFS keeps none: enabling is a no-op on a directory and EINVAL on
+	 * anything else, reading them is ENOTSUP. Before, the ENOTTY failed the lookup of every new file in On My iPhone
+	 * ("can't obtain VFSItem ... [25: ...]" for Safari's .download placeholder).
+	 */
+#define SWEET_APFSIOC_ENABLE_DIRSTATS      _IOW('J', 2, uint64_t)
+#define SWEET_APFSIOC_DIRSTAT              _IOWR('J', 32, uint8_t[40])
+	case SWEET_APFSIOC_ENABLE_DIRSTATS:
+		return vnode_isdir(vp) ? 0 : EINVAL;
+
+	case SWEET_APFSIOC_DIRSTAT:
+		return ENOTSUP;
 #endif
 
 	default:
